#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115139 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115310 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b936abcf-8e73-524c-a9bf-e59b55a48f5f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Even Exponents"}] :question/id #uuid "977cdc31-054e-5910-a649-e604dc4ce31f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8052" :question/problem "Find all of the real solutions to the equation $9x^4 = \\dfrac{1}{9}$." :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by isolating the $x^4$ term and then taking the $4$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $x^4$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9x^{4} &= \\frac{1}{9} \\\\\nx^{4} &= \\frac{1}{81}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $4$th root of each side and solve for $x$. Since the exponent $(4)$ is even, we consider both the positive and negative solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{4} &= \\frac{1}{81} \\\\\n\\sqrt[4]{x^{4}} &= ± \\sqrt[4]{\\frac{1}{81}} \\\\\nx &= ± \\sqrt[4]{(\\frac{1}{3})^{4}} \\\\\nx &= ± \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\dfrac13\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115140 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115311 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23e661ed-3a7b-598a-a7b1-fd5011fe4fb8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Containing an Expression Raised to an Even Power"}] :question/id #uuid "3f41b040-6584-57cd-8d47-b01e071b0fa9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8064" :question/problem "Find all of the real solutions to the equation $(x-3)^4=-\\dfrac{1}{81}$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\n(x-3)^4 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x$ because the exponent ($4$) is even. This expression can never be negative.\n\nTherefore, there are no real solutions to this equation."}]}
